# ============================================================
# Personal Health Graph — .gitignore
# ============================================================
# This file prevents accidental commits of personal health data.
# Template files (_TEMPLATE.md) and README files are tracked.
# User-created data files (dated entries, filled-in profiles) are not.
# ============================================================

# ----- Personal data files (NEVER commit these) -----

# Filled-in state files (contain personal health information)
# These are tracked as blank templates. IMPORTANT: because they are
# already tracked, uncommenting the lines below has no effect until
# you also untrack them: git rm --cached <file> (keeps your local copy).
# If you're using this repo as your working copy (not recommended),
# untrack each state file first, then uncomment its line:
# PROFILE.md
# MEDICATIONS.md
# EXPERIMENTS.md
# TIMELINE.md
# SUPPLEMENTS.md
# PROTOCOLS.md
# DOCTOR_QS.md
# EXPENSES.md
# LABS_HISTORY.md
# GENETICS.md

# Inbox (unprocessed files awaiting intake)
inbox/*
!inbox/README.md

# Dated log entries (symptoms, journal)
symptoms/[0-9]*.md
journal/[0-9]*.md

# Dated integration files (labs, wearables, genetics, etc.)
# Ignore everything in these dirs, then un-ignore README and _TEMPLATE
integrations/labs/*.md
integrations/genetics/*.md
integrations/wearable_daily/*.md
integrations/healthkit/*.md
integrations/microbiome/*.md
integrations/imaging/*.md
integrations/assessments/*.md
integrations/cycle/*.md
integrations/vitals/*.md
integrations/cgm/*.md
integrations/nutrition/*.md
!integrations/*/README.md
!integrations/*/_TEMPLATE.md

# Raw data exports (often large, always personal)
# Everything under integrations/raw/ is ignored regardless of format —
# PDFs, CSVs, XML exports, images, DICOM, genotype files, all of it.
# Only the README is tracked.
integrations/raw/**
!integrations/raw/README.md

# Generated reports (contain personal analysis)
# All report files are ignored except the README
reports/*
!reports/README.md

# NOTE: sample/ is fictional demo data and is intentionally tracked.
# The ignore patterns above are rooted paths and do not apply inside sample/.

# ----- OS and editor files -----
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.swp
*.swo
*~
.vscode/
.idea/

# ----- Environment and secrets -----
.env
.env.local
*.key
*.pem
# Personal reference docs (not part of the public template)
GITHUB_SETUP_GUIDE.md
DESIGN_PROVENANCE.md
